(6024354, 881204, 69325, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> beautiful blur. Too much competition for the brown this time. 3 members of my team outbrowned you! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>please don''t mistake this for an angry rant, this whole thing seems weird to me. So much has been spoken about "out of the box" or "non dpc friendly" shots which i think is great in theory. But this whole thing of always trying to compete for the bottom of the heap just mystifies me.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: beautiful blur. Too much competition for the brown this time. 3 members of my team outbrowned you!   please don''t mistake this for an angry rant, this whole thing seems weird to me. So much has been spoken about "out of the box" or "non dpc friendly" shots which i think is great in theory. But this whole thing of always trying to compete for the bottom of the heap just mystifies me.', '2010-05-24 14:39:30.000000', NULL, 0),
